- zh-cn/application-dev/reference/apis-ability-kit/capi-native-child-process-h.md, Gitee content blob SHA 2eb9308e9b4d043a9d1dca44738212edc768db9d.
- zh-cn/application-dev/application-models/capi-nativechildprocess-development-guideline.md, Gitee content blob SHA 5719a9112e1797d5ec8e7e188c6ef89018473b0c.
- Public API reference device behavior for OH_Ability_StartNativeChildProcess: API 13 and earlier support PC/2in1; API 14 and later support PC/2in1 and Tablet; other device types return NCP_ERR_NOT_SUPPORTED.
- Public API reference device behavior for OH_Ability_CreateNativeChildProcess: API 13 and earlier support PC/2in1; API 14 and later support PC/2in1 and Tablet; other device types return NCP_ERR_NOT_SUPPORTED.
- Public API reference enum mapping: NCP_ERR_NOT_SUPPORTED = 801, meaning Native child-process creation is unsupported.
- The public application-development procedure requires AbilityKit/native_child_process.h and libchild_process.so. It declares no application permission, debug mode, system-app privilege, enterprise ACL, or module/app manifest switch that can add phone support.
- The public documentation is the gate authority here. Header presence and successful linking alone are not treated as phone support.

